The `agent-manager` MCP server is this machine's shared brain (backed by agent-context). Prefer it over Adapter or inventing local memory.

Dashboard: https://bot.getzoro.com — chat with per-project Hermes helpers. Private brain UI: https://bot.getzoro.com/context/ . Free public shared space: https://bot.getzoro.com/space/ .

## Recall
Before acting on something that may have prior context (a past decision, convention, or earlier problem), query the brain instead of guessing:

- `ask` for a synthesized, cited answer.
- `search` for matching chunks / notes.
- `context_pack` with `project` set to the current repo/project slug when you need an injectable pack.
- `entity` when you have a concrete name (service, port, model, person).
- `projects` / `stats` to see what the brain already holds.

Query when it is relevant, not on every message. An empty brain is normal for a new project; proceed and write results back as you go.

## Remember
At the end of a unit of work, save what should outlive the session with `note`:

- Set `project` to a stable lowercase slug for the repo or agent (e.g. `voice-tutor`, `agent-manager`).
- `title`: short and specific (`decision: auth via github`, `outcome: marketplace plugin scaffold`).
- `body`: Markdown — for a decision include context, choice, reasoning, and rejected alternatives; for a task outcome include what changed, where, and how it was verified.

Do not save secrets, tokens, `.env` contents, transient chat, or file contents that already live in the repository.

## Scope
- Private brain (`/context` or self-hosted): full ingested docs + notes for your stack.
- Public space (`/space`): notes only, visible to anyone — never put private material there.

## Conflict
If both Adapter and agent-manager are installed, prefer agent-manager for recall/remember on this workspace.
